{%- comment -%}
  Casify product page: "The Shop Counter" (templates/product.convert.json).
  The familiar two-column product page set out as a candy counter: the real
  photos on a marble stage with a rail of candy-shop photo tickets; on the
  right a vendor ticket, the title, the rating row, a hanging brass price tag,
  style swatches, the model dropdown, candy-box pack tiers, the savings meter,
  Add to bag beside Buy now, the ship-by line, the service ribbon and two
  accordions.

  Commerce is shared with the Order Slip in assets/cv-product.js: the options
  resolve a real variant id, pack tiers set the quantity, and every pack price
  applies the tier's percentage the way the store's automatic discounts do
  ("Pack of 2 cases: 18% off", "Pack of 3 cases: 31% off"), so the page price
  is the checkout price. Buy now adds the same line and goes to checkout.

  Product ratings, here and in the Product structured data, come only from this
  product's Judge.me reviews by verified buyers (snippets/cv-jm-verified.liquid).
  Until one exists the row reads "No reviews yet". The store rating tickets and strip show a
  merchant-supplied store rating (the combined Google and Trustpilot figure, labelled
  as such) and never feed product review data.

  The offer tag uses the selected variant's compare-at price when one exists.
  Otherwise it may use the merchant-supplied fallback from this section. The
  percentage and amount saved are always calculated from the displayed prices.

  Low stock line reads the chosen variant's real inventory_quantity; it only
  shows for a variant Shopify tracks and stops selling at zero, under the
  merchant's own threshold, so it is never a fabricated urgency cue.

  Styles: assets/cv-pdp-counter.css. Zoom, ship-by date: assets/cv-pdp-counter.js.
  Motion: assets/cv-pdp-counter-motion.js.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'cv-pdp-counter.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'cv-pdp-extras.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- comment -%}
  The first 3D model (Model3d media) becomes the reel's second ticket: assets/cv-pdp-model.js, .css.
  Past the plan's cap of 250 videos and 3D models per store, a case's model is a plain file instead:
  the GLB in product.metafields.casify.model_glb and its still in .model_still (file references set by
  case_3d/file_models.py). It is not product media, so cards and the media order never see it. It opens
  in the same viewer, without "View in your space", which needs the USDZ Shopify makes only for Model3d.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign model_media = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'model' | first -%}
{%- assign model_file = nil -%}
{%- assign model_still = nil -%}
{%- if model_media == blank and product.metafields.casify.model_glb.value != blank -%}
  {%- assign model_file = product.metafields.casify.model_glb.value -%}
  {%- assign model_still = product.metafields.casify.model_still.value -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign has_model = false -%}
{%- if model_media != blank or model_file != blank -%}{%- assign has_model = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  model_alone: a case whose photos have not arrived from Printify yet shows its file model on
  its own, so the stage is never blank. model_stage: the stage carries a 3D viewer.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign model_alone = false -%}
{%- if model_file != blank and model_still != blank and product.media.size == 0 -%}{%- assign model_alone = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign model_stage = model_alone -%}
{%- if has_model and product.media.size > 1 -%}{%- assign model_stage = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if model_stage -%}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.shopify.com/shopifycloud/model-viewer-ui/assets/v1.0/model-viewer-ui.css" media="print" onload="this.media='all'">
  {{ 'cv-pdp-model.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- endif -%}
<script>
  /* Hide the tag, photo tickets and meter until cv-pdp-counter-motion.js has set their start
     states, and the promise stamps until cv-pdp-promises.js has. Never under reduced motion,
     and never for long. */
  (function (root) {
    if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
    root.classList.add('cvc-pending', 'cvc-promises-pending');
    setTimeout(function () { root.classList.remove('cvc-pending', 'cvc-promises-pending'); }, 1400);
  })(document.documentElement);
</script>

{%- liquid
  assign cvar = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  comment
    The phone-model option: named like one, or else the first option whose values name phones.
    Same test as snippets/cv-is-case.liquid. A product without one isn't a case (a candle, a
    cloth, a charm): it gets no packs, savings meter, protection meter or case features, since
    the pack discounts apply to cases only and the rest describes a case.
  endcomment
  assign model_oi = -1
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign oname = option.name | downcase
    if oname contains 'model' or oname contains 'phone' or oname contains 'device' or oname contains 'compatib' or oname contains 'applicable'
      assign model_oi = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor
  if model_oi == -1
    for option in product.options_with_values
      assign fv = option.values.first | downcase
      if fv contains 'iphone' or fv contains 'galaxy' or fv contains 'pixel' or fv contains 'samsung'
        assign model_oi = forloop.index0
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  assign is_case = false
  if model_oi >= 0
    assign is_case = true
  endif

  comment
    Model first (STORE-FACTS 4): a phone model is never chosen for the shopper. With more than one
    model value and no ?variant= in the URL (product.selected_variant), the picker prints a
    "Choose your phone model" placeholder and no phone; assets/cv-product.js keeps Add to bag and
    Buy now from posting until one is picked (cvs:needmodel).
  endcomment
  assign model_pending = false
  assign variant_label = cvar.title
  if model_oi >= 0
    assign model_values = product.options_with_values[model_oi].values
    if model_values.size > 1 and product.selected_variant == blank
      assign model_pending = true
      assign variant_label = ''
      for ov in cvar.options
        if forloop.index0 != model_oi
          if variant_label != ''
            assign variant_label = variant_label | append: ' / '
          endif
          assign variant_label = variant_label | append: ov
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif
  assign sold_suffix = 'products.buy.sold_out' | t | downcase | prepend: ' (' | append: ')'
  assign add_label = section.settings.cta_label
  if add_label == blank
    assign add_label = 'products.buy.add_to_bag' | t
  endif
  assign buy_label = section.settings.buy_label
  if buy_label == blank
    assign buy_label = 'products.buy.buy_now' | t
  endif
  assign sticky_label = section.settings.sticky_cta | default: add_label

  comment
    Case type, design name and phone brands, all read from the product itself (tags, title and the
    model option), so the short title, the feature chips and the case switcher only say what the
    product is. Magnetic is tested first: some magnetic cases carry the "tough case" tag too.
    Design name is the title before " Phone Case" ("Mistletoe Christmas"); products of one design
    share it, which is how the switcher finds the same print as another case type.
  endcomment
  assign case_type = ''
  if is_case
    assign type_tags = product.tags | join: '|' | downcase
    assign type_title = product.title | downcase
    if type_tags contains 'magnetic case' or type_title contains 'magnetic' or type_title contains 'magsafe'
      assign case_type = 'magnetic'
    elsif type_tags contains 'clear case' or type_title contains 'clear'
      assign case_type = 'clear'
    elsif type_tags contains 'tough case' or type_title contains 'tough'
      assign case_type = 'tough'
    endif
  endif
  assign case_label = ''
  if case_type != ''
    assign case_label = section.settings.case_label | default: '[type] case' | replace: '[type]', case_type | capitalize
  endif

  assign design_name = product.title | split: ' Phone Case' | first | strip
  if design_name == product.title
    assign design_name = product.title | split: ' | ' | first | strip
  endif
  assign short_title = false
  if section.settings.short_title and case_type != '' and design_name != blank and design_name != product.title
    assign short_title = true
  endif

  assign brands = ''
  if model_oi >= 0
    assign model_list = product.options_with_values[model_oi].values | join: '|' | downcase
    assign brand_list = ''
    if model_list contains 'iphone'
      assign brand_list = brand_list | append: '|iPhone'
    endif
    if model_list contains 'galaxy' or model_list contains 'samsung'
      assign brand_list = brand_list | append: '|Samsung'
    endif
    if model_list contains 'pixel'
      assign brand_list = brand_list | append: '|Pixel'
    endif
    assign brand_arr = brand_list | remove_first: '|' | split: '|'
    case brand_arr.size
      when 1
        assign brands = brand_arr.first
      when 2
        assign brands = brand_arr | join: ' & '
      when 3
        assign brands = brand_arr[0] | append: ', ' | append: brand_arr[1] | append: ' & ' | append: brand_arr[2]
    endcase
  endif
  assign title_sub = section.settings.title_sub | default: 'Phone case for [brands]'
  if brands == blank
    assign title_sub = title_sub | split: ' for ' | first
  else
    assign title_sub = title_sub | replace: '[brands]', brands
  endif

  assign chip_text = ''
  case case_type
    when 'tough'
      assign chip_text = section.settings.chips_tough
    when 'magnetic'
      assign chip_text = section.settings.chips_magnetic
    when 'clear'
      assign chip_text = section.settings.chips_clear
  endcase
  assign chips = chip_text | split: ','

  comment
    Each tier's percentage, by block position. Tiers of 2 and 3 cases read the theme settings
    (Packs and shipping: cv_pack_2_pct, cv_pack_3_pct), the one source of truth that must equal
    the automatic discounts in Shopify admin, unless the tier turns "use_theme_pct" off.
  endcomment
  assign tier_pcts = ''
  assign tier_count = 0
  assign active_i = -1
  assign first_i = -1
  assign max_pct = 0
  for b in section.blocks
    assign t_pct = 0
    if b.type == 'tier' and is_case
      assign t_pct = b.settings.discount_pct | default: 0
      if b.settings.use_theme_pct != false
        if b.settings.qty == 2 and settings.cv_pack_2_pct != blank
          assign t_pct = settings.cv_pack_2_pct
        elsif b.settings.qty == 3 and settings.cv_pack_3_pct != blank
          assign t_pct = settings.cv_pack_3_pct
        endif
      endif
      assign tier_count = tier_count | plus: 1
      if t_pct > max_pct
        assign max_pct = t_pct
      endif
      if first_i == -1
        assign first_i = forloop.index0
      endif
      if active_i == -1 and b.settings.default_checked
        assign active_i = forloop.index0
      endif
    endif
    assign tier_pcts = tier_pcts | append: t_pct | append: ','
  endfor
  assign pct_arr = tier_pcts | split: ','
  if active_i == -1
    assign active_i = first_i
  endif

  assign active_tier = nil
  assign active_qty = 1
  assign active_pct = 0
  if active_i >= 0
    assign active_tier = section.blocks[active_i]
    assign active_qty = active_tier.settings.qty | at_least: 1
    assign active_pct = pct_arr[active_i] | plus: 0
  endif

  comment
    Shopify takes a percentage discount off the line and rounds to the cent, so the page does too.
  endcomment
  assign active_line = cvar.price | times: active_qty
  assign active_off = active_line | times: active_pct | divided_by: 100.0 | floor
  assign active_total = active_line | minus: active_off

  comment
    The fallback compare-at price is typed in the shop currency, so it applies only when the
    shopper pays in that currency (Shopify Markets would otherwise compare unlike amounts).
  endcomment
  assign compare_fallback = 0
  if section.settings.compare_price_fallback != blank and cart.currency.iso_code == shop.currency
    assign compare_fallback = section.settings.compare_price_fallback | times: 100 | round
  endif
  assign compare_price = cvar.compare_at_price | default: 0
  if compare_price <= cvar.price and compare_fallback > cvar.price
    assign compare_price = compare_fallback
  endif
  assign show_compare = false
  assign compare_savings = 0
  assign compare_discount = 0
  if compare_price > cvar.price
    assign show_compare = true
    assign compare_savings = compare_price | minus: cvar.price
    assign compare_discount = compare_savings | times: 100.0 | divided_by: compare_price | round
  endif

  assign next_tier = nil
  assign next_pct = 0
  for b in section.blocks
    assign b_pct = pct_arr[forloop.index0] | plus: 0
    if b.type == 'tier' and b_pct > active_pct
      if next_tier == nil or b_pct < next_pct
        assign next_tier = b
        assign next_pct = b_pct
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign meter_pct = 0
  if max_pct > 0
    assign meter_pct = active_pct | times: 100.0 | divided_by: max_pct | round
  endif

  comment
    Ratings: this product's Judge.me reviews by verified buyers only (snippets/cv-jm-verified.liquid).
    No reviews, no stars: an empty product shows no star fill (PRODUCT.md:102, STORE-FACTS 7, gate G1).
  endcomment
  capture jm_stats
    render 'cv-jm-verified', mode: 'stats', scope: 'product', handle: product.handle
  endcapture
  assign jm_parts = jm_stats | split: '␟'
  assign rating_count = jm_parts[0] | plus: 0
  assign rating_value = 0
  assign star_pct = 0
  assign has_rating = false
  if rating_count > 0
    assign has_rating = true
    assign rating_value = jm_parts[1] | plus: 0 | times: 1.0 | divided_by: rating_count
    assign star_pct = rating_value | times: 20.0 | round: 1
  endif

  comment
    Low stock: only for a variant Shopify itself is tracking, only while it's
    actually in stock, and only under the merchant's own threshold. Never
    shown for untracked inventory or "continue selling" variants, where a
    count would not be a real number.
  endcomment
  assign show_stock = false
  assign stock_qty = 0
  if section.settings.low_stock_threshold > 0 and cvar.inventory_management == 'shopify' and cvar.inventory_policy == 'deny' and cvar.inventory_quantity > 0 and cvar.inventory_quantity <= section.settings.low_stock_threshold
    assign show_stock = true
    assign stock_qty = cvar.inventory_quantity
  endif
  assign stock_text = section.settings.low_stock_text | replace: '[qty]', stock_qty

  comment
    Breadcrumb: the collection the shopper came from, else the product's first real
    category; never the store's front-page collection ("Home page").
  endcomment
  assign crumb_collection = false
  if collection != blank and collection.handle != 'frontpage'
    assign crumb_collection = collection
  else
    for c in product.collections
      if c.handle != 'frontpage'
        assign crumb_collection = c
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  assign hero_media = cvar.featured_media | default: product.featured_media
  assign hero_image = hero_media.preview_image | default: hero_media
  assign gallery_count = product.media.size | at_most: 8
  comment
    The model ticket replaces the model's own slot when it is among the first 8,
    otherwise it takes the 8th photo's, so the reel never grows past 8 tickets.
  endcomment
  assign photo_limit = 8
  if model_media != blank and model_media.position > 8
    assign photo_limit = 7
  endif
  comment
    A file model is not in product.media, so its ticket always takes the 8th photo's place.
  endcomment
  if model_file != blank
    assign photo_limit = 7
  endif
  comment
    "Open on the 3D view": the model ticket comes first and the stage opens on the
    viewer. Its preview picture paints first, the live model replaces it once loaded.
  endcomment
  assign model_main = model_alone
  if has_model and product.media.size > 1 and section.settings.model_first
    assign model_main = true
  endif
  assign stage_image = hero_image
  assign stage_alt = hero_media.alt | default: product.title
  if model_main and model_media.preview_image != blank
    assign stage_image = model_media.preview_image
    assign stage_alt = model_media.alt | default: product.title
  elsif model_main and model_still != blank
    assign stage_image = model_still
    assign stage_alt = model_still.alt | default: product.title
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%} Only the variant fields the scripts read (snippets/cv-variants-json.liquid): 162 KB of HTML down to about 33 KB on a 98-variant case. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture cv_variants -%}{%- render 'cv-variants-json', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}

<section class="cvc" id="cvPdp" data-cv-pdp="counter"
         data-variants="{{ cv_variants | strip | escape }}"
         data-current-options="{{ cvar.options | json | escape }}"
         data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}"
         data-model-index="{{ model_oi }}"
         data-max-pct="{{ max_pct }}"
         data-compare-at-fallback="{{ compare_fallback }}"
         data-cv-model-confirmed="{% if model_pending %}false{% else %}true{% endif %}"
         data-i18n-adding="{{ 'products.buy.adding' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-added="{{ 'products.buy.added' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-try-again="{{ 'products.buy.try_again' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-to-checkout="{{ 'products.buy.to_checkout' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-checkout-redirect="{{ 'products.buy.checkout_redirect' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-unavailable="{{ 'products.buy.unavailable' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-each="{{ 'products.buy.each' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-sold-out="{{ 'products.buy.sold_out' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-error="{{ 'products.buy.error' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-choose-model="{{ 'products.buy.choose_model' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-model-placeholder="{{ 'products.buy.model_placeholder' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-added-one="{{ 'products.buy.added_one' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-added-many="{{ 'products.buy.added_many' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-mixed="{{ 'products.buy.mixed' | t | escape }}"
         data-i18n-add-to-bag="{{ add_label | escape }}"
         data-i18n-buy-now="{{ buy_label | escape }}"
         style="--cvc-box: url('{{ 'pdp-counter-box.webp' | asset_url }}'); --cvc-box-teal: url('{{ 'pdp-counter-box-teal.webp' | asset_url }}');">
  <div class="cvc__inner">
    <nav class="cvc__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ 'general.breadcrumbs.home' | t }}</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      {%- if crumb_collection != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ crumb_collection.url }}">{{ crumb_collection.title | escape }}</a>
      {%- else -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">{{ section.settings.crumb_label | default: 'Cases' | escape }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">{{ product.title | escape }}</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="cvc__grid">
      {%- comment -%} ================= Photos: candy-shop ticket rail + marble stage ================= {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="cvc__gallery{% if product.media.size <= 1 %} cvc__gallery--single{% endif %}">
        {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
          <div class="cvc__photo-reel-shell">
            <span class="cvc__photo-reel-track cvc__photo-reel-track--vertical" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 320" preserveAspectRatio="none" focusable="false">
                <path class="cvc__photo-reel-shadow" d="M12 7V313"/>
                <path class="cvc__photo-reel-cream" d="M12 7V313"/>
                <path class="cvc__photo-reel-stripe" data-cvc-reel-path d="M12 7V313"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <span class="cvc__photo-reel-track cvc__photo-reel-track--horizontal" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 320 24" preserveAspectRatio="none" focusable="false">
                <path class="cvc__photo-reel-shadow" d="M7 12H313"/>
                <path class="cvc__photo-reel-cream" d="M7 12H313"/>
                <path class="cvc__photo-reel-stripe" data-cvc-reel-path d="M7 12H313"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <img
              class="cvc__photo-reel-sweet cvc__photo-reel-sweet--start"
              src="{{ 'hero-sweet-wrapped-red.webp' | asset_url }}"
              width="440"
              height="212"
              alt=""
              loading="eager"
              decoding="async"
            >
            {%- assign hero_thumb_index = 1 -%}
            {%- if has_model -%}
              {%- if model_main -%}{%- assign model_n = 1 -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign model_n = 2 -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign mpic = model_media.preview_image | default: model_still -%}
              {%- capture model_ticket -%}
                <button type="button" class="cvc__photo-ticket cvc__photo-ticket--3d" id="cvcThumb-{{ section.id }}-{{ model_n }}" role="tab" data-cv-thumb data-cv-model
                        aria-selected="{{ model_main }}"
                        aria-controls="cvcMedia-{{ section.id }}"
                        tabindex="{% if model_main %}0{% else %}-1{% endif %}"
                        aria-label="3D view, {{ 'products.gallery.photo_count' | t: index: model_n, count: gallery_count }}"
                        {%- if mpic != blank %}
                        data-cv-full="{{ mpic | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
                        data-cv-zoom="{{ mpic | image_url: width: 2400 }}"{% endif %}>
                  <span class="cvc__photo-ticket-card">
                    <svg class="cvc__photo-ticket-frame" viewBox="0 0 96 108" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                      <path class="cvc__photo-ticket-paper" d="M13 3H83C83 8 87 12 93 12V96C87 96 83 100 83 105H13C13 100 9 96 3 96V12C9 12 13 8 13 3Z"/>
                      <path class="cvc__photo-ticket-outline" d="M13 3H83C83 8 87 12 93 12V96C87 96 83 100 83 105H13C13 100 9 96 3 96V12C9 12 13 8 13 3Z"/>
                      <path class="cvc__photo-ticket-perf" d="M13 86H83"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span class="cvc__photo-ticket-image">{%- if mpic != blank -%}{{ mpic | image_url: width: 240 | image_tag: width: 160, height: 160, alt: '', loading: 'lazy' }}{%- endif -%}</span>
                    <span class="cvc__photo-ticket-3d" aria-hidden="true">3D</span>
                    <span class="cvc__photo-ticket-no" aria-hidden="true">{{ model_n }}</span>
                  </span>
                </button>
              {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            <div class="cvc__photo-reel" role="tablist" aria-label="{{ 'products.gallery.photos' | t }}">
              {%- assign n = 0 -%}
              {%- if model_main -%}{%- assign n = 1 -%}{{ model_ticket }}{%- endif -%}
              {%- for media in product.media limit: photo_limit -%}
                {%- if media.media_type == 'model' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- if media.media_type == 'image' or media.preview_image -%}
                  {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}
                  {%- assign pic = media.preview_image | default: media -%}
                  {%- assign is_hero = false -%}
                  {%- if model_main == false and media.id == hero_media.id -%}{%- assign is_hero = true -%}{%- assign hero_thumb_index = n -%}{%- endif -%}
                  <button type="button" class="cvc__photo-ticket" id="cvcThumb-{{ section.id }}-{{ n }}" role="tab" data-cv-thumb
                          aria-selected="{{ is_hero }}"
                          aria-controls="cvcMedia-{{ section.id }}"
                          tabindex="{% if is_hero %}0{% else %}-1{% endif %}"
                          aria-label="{{ 'products.gallery.photo_count' | t: index: n, count: gallery_count }}"
                          data-cv-full="{{ pic | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
                          data-cv-zoom="{{ pic | image_url: width: 2400 }}">
                    <span class="cvc__photo-ticket-card">
                      <svg class="cvc__photo-ticket-frame" viewBox="0 0 96 108" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                        <path class="cvc__photo-ticket-paper" d="M13 3H83C83 8 87 12 93 12V96C87 96 83 100 83 105H13C13 100 9 96 3 96V12C9 12 13 8 13 3Z"/>
                        <path class="cvc__photo-ticket-outline" d="M13 3H83C83 8 87 12 93 12V96C87 96 83 100 83 105H13C13 100 9 96 3 96V12C9 12 13 8 13 3Z"/>
                        <path class="cvc__photo-ticket-perf" d="M13 86H83"/>
                      </svg>
                      <span class="cvc__photo-ticket-image">{{ pic | image_url: width: 240 | image_tag: width: 160, height: 160, alt: '', loading: 'lazy' }}</span>
                      <span class="cvc__photo-ticket-no" aria-hidden="true">{{ n }}</span>
                    </span>
                  </button>
                  {%- if n == 1 and has_model and model_main == false -%}
                    {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}
                    {{ model_ticket }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
            <img
              class="cvc__photo-reel-sweet cvc__photo-reel-sweet--end"
              src="{{ 'hero-sweet-wrapped-teal.webp' | asset_url }}"
              width="440"
              height="164"
              alt=""
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            >
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="cvc__stage cvc__stage--awning-{{ section.settings.show_awning }}{% if model_main %} is-3d{% endif %}"{% if product.media.size > 1 %} id="cvcMedia-{{ section.id }}" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="cvcThumb-{{ section.id }}-{{ hero_thumb_index }}"{% endif %}>
          {%- render 'cv-awning', show: section.settings.show_awning, stripes: section.settings.awning_stripes, tone: section.settings.awning_tone, swipe: section.settings.awning_swipe -%}
          {%- render 'cv-photo-price', show: section.settings.show_photo_price, variant: cvar -%}
          {%- if stage_image != blank -%}
            {{ stage_image | image_url: width: 1400 | image_tag:
                widths: '600, 900, 1200, 1400',
                sizes: '(min-width: 1270px) 520px, (min-width: 990px) 44vw, calc(100vw - 32px)',
                class: 'cvc__photo', id: 'cvMainImage',
                alt: stage_alt,
                loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high' }}
            <button type="button" class="cvc__zoom" data-cvc-zoom-open aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="cvcZoom-{{ section.id }}"
                    data-cv-zoom="{{ stage_image | image_url: width: 2400 }}">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.4 15.4 21 21"/></svg>
              <span>{%- if section.settings.zoom_label != blank -%}{{ section.settings.zoom_label | escape }}{%- else -%}{{ 'products.gallery.zoom' | t }}{%- endif -%}</span>
            </button>
            {%- if model_stage -%}
              <div class="cvc__model" data-cvc-model{% unless model_main %} hidden{% endunless %}>
                {%- comment -%}
                  Neutral lighting keeps pale prints their real colour; the default room light washes them to white.
                  A file model gets the same <model-viewer> that model_viewer_tag prints for Model3d media.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if model_media != blank -%}
                  <template>{{ model_media | model_viewer_tag: image_size: '1400x', reveal: 'auto', camera-orbit: '-25deg 75deg auto', shadow-intensity: '1', environment-image: 'neutral', alt: model_media.alt }}</template>
                  <button type="button" class="cvc__xr" data-shopify-xr data-shopify-model3d-id="{{ model_media.id }}" data-shopify-title="{{ product.title | escape }}" data-shopify-xr-hidden>
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2.5 20.5 7v10L12 21.5 3.5 17V7z"/><path d="M3.5 7 12 11.5 20.5 7M12 11.5v10"/></svg>
                    <span>{{ 'products.gallery.view_in_space' | t }}</span>
                  </button>
                  <script type="application/json" data-cvc-model-json>{{ product.media | where: 'media_type', 'model' | json }}</script>
                {%- else -%}
                  <template><model-viewer reveal="auto" camera-orbit="-25deg 75deg auto" shadow-intensity="1" environment-image="neutral" alt="{{ model_file.alt | default: model_still.alt | default: product.title | escape }}" src="{{ model_file.url }}" camera-controls="true" style="--poster-color: transparent;" data-shopify-feature="1.12"{% if model_still != blank %} poster="{{ model_still | image_url: width: 1400 }}"{% endif %}></model-viewer></template>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              <script src="{{ 'cv-pdp-model.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="cvc__photo cvc__photo--empty" id="cvMainImage" role="img" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}"></span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ================= The counter: buy box ================= {%- endcomment -%}
      <form class="cvc__box" id="cvAddForm" method="post" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}">
        {%- comment -%}
          Without JavaScript the form posts natively: the <noscript> variant list below is the only
          field named "id", so a shopper picks the real case (model first) and the native post can
          never add a phone they did not choose. With JavaScript, assets/cv-product.js keeps
          #cvVariantId in step and posts the chosen cases to /cart/add.js itself.
          The packs, the savings meter and the per-case rows only work with JavaScript, so they hide
          under html.no-js (cv-pdp-counter.css) and the native post always adds one case; cv-product.js
          writes the pack's quantity here when it runs.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <input type="hidden" id="cvVariantId" value="{% unless model_pending %}{{ cvar.id }}{% endunless %}">
        <input type="hidden" name="quantity" id="cvQuantity" value="1">

        {%- if short_title -%}
          <p class="cvc__vendor">{{ case_label | escape }}</p>
        {%- elsif product.vendor != blank -%}
          <p class="cvc__vendor">{{ product.vendor | escape }}{% if section.settings.vendor_suffix != blank and is_case %} {{ section.settings.vendor_suffix | escape }}{% endif %}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The brass price tag by the title ("Hanging price tag by the title").
          Off, the price still shows in the summary under the title; the
          scripts that update the tag skip it when it isn't there.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.show_price_tag -%}
        <p class="cvc__tag">
          <img class="cvc__tag-plate" src="{{ 'pdp-counter-tag.webp' | asset_url }}" width="360" height="414" alt="" loading="eager">
          <span class="cvc__tag-price" aria-live="polite">
            <span id="cvPriceNow"><span class="cvc__visually-hidden">{{ 'products.price_offer.now' | t }}: </span>{{ cvar.price | money }}</span>
            <s id="cvPriceWas"{% unless show_compare %} hidden{% endunless %}><span class="cvc__visually-hidden">{{ 'products.price_offer.compare_at' | t }}: </span>{{ compare_price | money }}</s>
          </span>
          <span class="cvc__tag-sale" data-cv-tag-sale{% unless show_compare %} hidden{% endunless %} aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" focusable="false">
              <path d="M50 3 59 12 72 8 77 21 91 23 88 37 98 47 89 58 93 72 79 77 76 91 62 88 51 98 41 89 27 93 22 79 8 76 12 62 2 51 11 41 7 27 21 22 24 8 38 12Z"/>
              <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="34"/>
            </svg>
            <span class="cvc__tag-sale-copy"><strong data-cv-discount-pct>{{ compare_discount }}%</strong><small>{{ 'products.price_offer.off' | t }}</small></span>
          </span>
        </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Short title: the design name large, what it is in a smaller line under it. Both sit in the
          h1, so the heading still names the product in full for search; the page title and the
          product schema keep the full Shopify title.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if short_title -%}
          <h1 class="cvc__title">{{ design_name | escape }} <span class="cvc__title-sub">{{ title_sub | escape }}</span></h1>
        {%- else -%}
          <h1 class="cvc__title">{{ product.title | escape }}</h1>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- render 'cv-counter-blocks', blocks: section.blocks, type: 'summary', product: product, variant: cvar, settings: section.settings -%}

        {%- comment -%} What this case type is, from the section's chips for that type. Facts true for every case of the type only. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if chips.size > 0 -%}
          <ul class="cvc__chips" role="list" aria-label="{{ case_label | escape }}">
            {%- for chip in chips -%}
              {%- assign chip = chip | strip -%}
              {%- if chip != blank -%}
                <li class="cvc__chip"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5 10 17.5 19 7"/></svg>{{ chip | escape }}</li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}

        <p class="cvc__price-saving cvc__price-saving--{{ section.settings.show_price_saving }}" data-cv-price-proof aria-live="polite"{% unless show_compare %} hidden{% endunless %}>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 13 13 20 4 11V4h7l9 9Z"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.25"/></svg>
          <span>{{ 'products.price_offer.you_save' | t }}</span>
          <strong data-cv-price-save>{{ compare_savings | money }}</strong>
        </p>

        {%- assign service_count = 0 -%}
        {%- for b in section.blocks -%}{%- if b.type == 'service' -%}{%- assign service_count = service_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
        {%- if service_count > 0 -%}
          {%- comment -%} Shop promises as postage stamps. Motion and the three.js van, return loop and packing box: assets/cv-pdp-promises.js; the SVGs are the still fallback. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="cvc__promises" data-cvc-promises>
            <ul class="cvc__promises-list" role="list">
              {%- for b in section.blocks -%}
                {%- if b.type == 'service' -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign promise_icon = 'truck'
                    if b.settings.icon == 'returns' or b.settings.icon == 'box'
                      assign promise_icon = b.settings.icon
                    endif
                  -%}
                  <li class="cvc__promise cvc__promise--{{ promise_icon }}" data-cvc-promise="{{ promise_icon }}" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <span class="cvc__promise-art" data-cvc-promise-art aria-hidden="true">
                      {%- case promise_icon -%}
                        {%- when 'returns' -%}
                          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11a8 8 0 0 1 14-5"/><path d="M18 3v3.5h-3.5"/><path d="M20 13a8 8 0 0 1-14 5"/><path d="M6 21v-3.5h3.5"/></svg>
                        {%- when 'box' -%}
                          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false"><path d="M12 2.8 20 7v10l-8 4.2L4 17V7z"/><path d="m4 7 8 4.2L20 7"/><path d="M12 11.2v10"/><path d="m8 4.9 8 4.2"/></svg>
                        {%- else -%}
                          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 6.5h10.5v9H2.5z"/><path d="M13 9.5h4.2l3.3 3.4v2.6H13z"/><circle cx="6.5" cy="17.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="1.9"/></svg>
                      {%- endcase -%}
                    </span>
                    <span class="cvc__promise-text">{{ b.settings.text | escape }}</span>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.show_rating -%}
          <a class="cvc__rating" href="#{{ section.settings.reviews_anchor | default: 'cvc-reviews' | remove: '#' | escape }}" data-cvc-rating>
            {%- comment -%}
              Gate G1 (PLAN.md 4; PRODUCT.md:102-105): no stars without the product's own reviews, and the
              typed "Customer proof text" shows only when "show_customer_proof" is on. Not in the store's
              evidence on hand, so it is off by default and the row reads "No reviews yet".
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if has_rating -%}
              {%- render 'cv-stars', fill: star_pct, class: 'cvc__stars' -%}
              {%- assign rating_shown = rating_value | round: 1 -%}
              <span class="cvc__rating-text" data-cvc-rating-text><span aria-hidden="true">{{ rating_shown }}</span> <span class="cvc__visually-hidden">{{ 'products.rating.out_of' | t: rating: rating_shown }}, </span><span class="cvc__rating-separator" aria-hidden="true">·</span><u>{% if rating_count == 1 %}{{ 'products.rating.reviews_one' | t: count: rating_count }}{% else %}{{ 'products.rating.reviews_other' | t: count: rating_count }}{% endif %}</u></span>
            {%- else -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign proof_text = 'products.rating.no_reviews_yet' | t
                if section.settings.show_customer_proof and section.settings.empty_rating_text != blank
                  assign proof_text = section.settings.empty_rating_text
                endif
                assign proof_link = section.settings.empty_rating_link
                if proof_link == blank
                  assign proof_link = 'products.rating.write_first_review' | t
                endif
              -%}
              <span class="cvc__rating-text" data-cvc-rating-text>{{ proof_text | escape }}<span class="cvc__rating-separator" aria-hidden="true">·</span><u>{{ proof_link | escape }}</u></span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Google and Trustpilot tickets sit under the price, inside the "Rating, price &
          pitch" block. Without that block they show here instead.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign has_summary = false -%}
        {%- for b in section.blocks -%}{%- if b.type == 'summary' -%}{%- assign has_summary = true -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
        {%- unless has_summary -%}
          {%- render 'cv-store-ratings', settings: section.settings -%}
        {%- endunless -%}

        <p class="cvc__stock cvc__stock--{{ section.settings.stock_style | default: 'pill' }}" data-cvc-stock role="status" aria-atomic="true"
           data-threshold="{{ section.settings.low_stock_threshold }}"
           data-template="{{ section.settings.low_stock_text | escape }}"
           {% unless show_stock %}hidden{% endunless %}>
          <span class="cvc__stock-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span data-cvc-stock-text>{{ stock_text }}</span>
        </p>

        {%- comment -%} Sales notes share one wrapper: assets/cv-pdp-sales.js rolls their numbers up and draws the three.js flame and rocket over it. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture sales_notes -%}{%- render 'cv-counter-blocks', blocks: section.blocks, type: 'sales_note', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- if sales_notes != blank -%}
          <div class="cvc__sales" data-cvc-sales>{{ sales_notes }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == '@app' -%}<div class="cvc__app">{% render block %}</div>{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          ---------- Case switcher: this design as Tough, Magnetic and Clear ----------
          The other case types are separate products with the same design name, so no product or
          metafield has to be linked by hand; a design sold as one type only shows no switcher.
          Found by handle first: every case so far was listed by the same Printify flow, so a
          design's three handles differ only in their ending, in one of two families (2026-11-09:
          148 designs end -pixel-tough-case / -magnetic-impact-resistant-case /
          -clear-impact-resistant-case, 15 end -tough-case / -magsafe-compatible-tough-case /
          -clear-impact-case). Two all_products lookups load two products, about 0.1 s of server
          time, where reading the catalogue in one page of 250 (collections.all) took about 2.4 s
          on every uncached product page and missed designs listed after the 250th product.
          A product found by handle must pass the same design-name and type checks as the scan.
          The scan still runs when the handle has neither family's ending or neither lookup finds
          a sibling, so a case listed some other way keeps its switcher.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.show_case_switcher and case_type != '' -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign sib_tough = nil
            assign sib_magnetic = nil
            assign sib_clear = nil
            case case_type
              when 'tough'
                assign sib_tough = product
              when 'magnetic'
                assign sib_magnetic = product
              when 'clear'
                assign sib_clear = product
            endcase

            assign sw_stem = ''
            assign sw_ends = ''
            assign sw_endings = '-magnetic-impact-resistant-case|-clear-impact-resistant-case|-pixel-tough-case|-magsafe-compatible-tough-case|-clear-impact-case|-tough-case' | split: '|'
            for sw_end in sw_endings
              assign sw_len = sw_end | size
              assign sw_from = 0 | minus: sw_len
              assign sw_tail = product.handle | slice: sw_from, sw_len
              if sw_tail == sw_end
                assign sw_keep = product.handle | size | minus: sw_len
                assign sw_stem = product.handle | slice: 0, sw_keep
                if forloop.index <= 3
                  assign sw_ends = '-pixel-tough-case|-magnetic-impact-resistant-case|-clear-impact-resistant-case' | split: '|'
                else
                  assign sw_ends = '-tough-case|-magsafe-compatible-tough-case|-clear-impact-case' | split: '|'
                endif
                break
              endif
            endfor

            assign sw_found = 0
            if sw_stem != ''
              for sw_end in sw_ends
                assign sw_handle = sw_stem | append: sw_end
                if sw_handle == product.handle
                  continue
                endif
                assign p = all_products[sw_handle]
                if p.id == blank or p.id == product.id
                  continue
                endif
                assign p_name = p.title | split: ' Phone Case' | first | strip
                if p_name == p.title
                  assign p_name = p.title | split: ' | ' | first | strip
                endif
                if p_name != design_name
                  continue
                endif
                assign p_tags = p.tags | join: '|' | downcase
                assign p_title = p.title | downcase
                if p_tags contains 'magnetic case' or p_title contains 'magnetic' or p_title contains 'magsafe'
                  if sib_magnetic == nil
                    assign sib_magnetic = p
                    assign sw_found = sw_found | plus: 1
                  endif
                elsif p_tags contains 'clear case' or p_title contains 'clear'
                  if sib_clear == nil
                    assign sib_clear = p
                    assign sw_found = sw_found | plus: 1
                  endif
                elsif p_tags contains 'tough case' or p_title contains 'tough'
                  if sib_tough == nil
                    assign sib_tough = p
                    assign sw_found = sw_found | plus: 1
                  endif
                endif
              endfor
            endif
          -%}
          {%- if sw_found == 0 -%}
          {%- paginate collections.all.products by 250 -%}
            {%- for p in collections.all.products -%}
              {%- liquid
                if p.id == product.id
                  continue
                endif
                assign p_name = p.title | split: ' Phone Case' | first | strip
                if p_name == p.title
                  assign p_name = p.title | split: ' | ' | first | strip
                endif
                if p_name != design_name
                  continue
                endif
                assign p_tags = p.tags | join: '|' | downcase
                assign p_title = p.title | downcase
                if p_tags contains 'magnetic case' or p_title contains 'magnetic' or p_title contains 'magsafe'
                  if sib_magnetic == nil
                    assign sib_magnetic = p
                  endif
                elsif p_tags contains 'clear case' or p_title contains 'clear'
                  if sib_clear == nil
                    assign sib_clear = p
                  endif
                elsif p_tags contains 'tough case' or p_title contains 'tough'
                  if sib_tough == nil
                    assign sib_tough = p
                  endif
                endif
              -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endpaginate -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign type_count = 0
            if sib_tough
              assign type_count = type_count | plus: 1
            endif
            if sib_magnetic
              assign type_count = type_count | plus: 1
            endif
            if sib_clear
              assign type_count = type_count | plus: 1
            endif
          -%}
          {%- if type_count > 1 -%}
            <div class="cvc__opt cvc__opt--types">
              <p class="cvc__label" id="cvcTypes-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.switcher_label | default: 'Case' | escape }}: <span class="cvc__label-value">{{ case_label | escape }}</span></p>
              <ul class="cvc__types" role="list" aria-labelledby="cvcTypes-{{ section.id }}" style="--cvc-types: {{ type_count }};">
                {%- for t in (1..3) -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    case t
                      when 1
                        assign tp = sib_tough
                        assign tp_name = 'Tough'
                      when 2
                        assign tp = sib_magnetic
                        assign tp_name = 'Magnetic'
                      when 3
                        assign tp = sib_clear
                        assign tp_name = 'Clear'
                    endcase
                  -%}
                  {%- if tp -%}
                    <li>
                      <a class="cvc__type" href="{{ tp.url }}"{% if tp.id == product.id %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                        <span class="cvc__type-pic">
                          {%- if tp.featured_image -%}{{ tp.featured_image | image_url: width: 120 | image_tag: width: 44, height: 44, alt: '', loading: 'lazy' }}{%- endif -%}
                        </span>
                        <span class="cvc__type-name">{{ tp_name }}</span>
                        {%- comment -%} Availability is per market: Magnetic and Clear ship to the US and Canada only, so elsewhere they read sold out. {%- endcomment -%}
                        <span class="cvc__type-price">{% if tp.available %}{{ tp.price_min | money }}{% else %}{{ 'products.buy.sold_out' | t }}{% endif %}</span>
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---------- The non-model options: swatches when every value has its own photo ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
          {%- assign oi = forloop.index0 -%}
          {%- if oi != model_oi and option.values.size > 0 -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign line_label = option.name
              if section.settings.option_label != blank
                assign line_label = section.settings.option_label
              endif
              assign swatch_photos = true
              for value in option.values
                assign found = false
                for v in product.variants
                  if v.options[oi] == value and v.featured_image
                    assign found = true
                    break
                  endif
                endfor
                unless found
                  assign swatch_photos = false
                  break
                endunless
              endfor
            -%}
            <div class="cvc__opt">
              <p class="cvc__label" id="cvcOpt{{ oi }}-{{ section.id }}">{{ line_label | escape }}: <span class="cvc__label-value" data-cv-opt-out="{{ oi }}">{{ cvar.options[oi] | escape }}</span></p>
              <div class="cvc__swatches{% unless swatch_photos %} cvc__swatches--text{% endunless %}" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="cvcOpt{{ oi }}-{{ section.id }}">
                {%- for value in option.values -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign vmatch = nil
                    assign vpic = nil
                    for v in product.variants
                      if v.options[oi] == value
                        if vmatch == nil
                          assign vmatch = v
                        endif
                        if vpic == nil and v.featured_image
                          assign vpic = v.featured_image
                        endif
                        if v.available
                          assign vmatch = v
                          if vpic != nil
                            break
                          endif
                        endif
                      endif
                    endfor
                  -%}
                  <button type="button" class="cvc__swatch" role="radio"
                          aria-checked="{% if cvar.options[oi] == value %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                          tabindex="{% if cvar.options[oi] == value %}0{% else %}-1{% endif %}"
                          {% if swatch_photos %}aria-label="{{ value | escape }}" title="{{ value | escape }}"{% endif %}
                          data-cv-option-index="{{ oi }}"
                          data-cv-value="{{ value | escape }}"
                          data-cv-stock="{% unless vmatch.available %}out{% endunless %}">
                    {%- if swatch_photos -%}
                      {{ vpic | image_url: width: 140 | image_tag: width: 70, height: 70, alt: '', loading: 'lazy' }}
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{ value | escape }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---------- Protection meter: impact and thickness bars (snippets/cv-spec-meter.liquid) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if is_case -%}{%- render 'cv-counter-blocks', blocks: section.blocks, type: 'spec_meter', product: product -%}{%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---------- The phone model: a native dropdown, every value this case is made for ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if model_oi >= 0 -%}
          {%- assign model_option = product.options_with_values[model_oi] -%}
          <div class="cvc__opt cvc__opt--model">
            <label class="cvc__label" for="cvcModel-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.model_label | default: 'Model' | escape }}</label>
            <span class="cvc__select">
              <select id="cvcModel-{{ section.id }}" name="options[{{ model_option.name | escape }}]" data-cv-option-index="{{ model_oi }}" data-sold-suffix="{{ sold_suffix | escape }}">
                {%- if model_pending -%}
                  <option value="" disabled selected data-cv-placeholder>{{ 'products.buy.model_placeholder' | t }}</option>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- for value in model_option.values -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign vmatch = nil
                    for v in product.variants
                      if v.options[model_oi] == value
                        if vmatch == nil
                          assign vmatch = v
                        endif
                        if v.available
                          assign vmatch = v
                          break
                        endif
                      endif
                    endfor
                  -%}
                  <option value="{{ value | escape }}"{% if model_pending == false and cvar.options[model_oi] == value %} selected{% endif %}>{{ value | escape }}{% unless vmatch.available %}{{ sold_suffix }}{% endunless %}</option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---------- Without JavaScript: one native list of real cases (the custom pickers hide under html.no-js) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
        <noscript>
          {%- if product.has_only_default_variant -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ cvar.id }}">
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="cvc__opt cvc__opt--noscript">
              <label class="cvc__label" for="cvcVariant-{{ section.id }}">{{ product.options | join: ' / ' | escape }}</label>
              <span class="cvc__select">
                <select id="cvcVariant-{{ section.id }}" name="id" required>
                  {%- if model_oi >= 0 and product.options_with_values[model_oi].values.size > 1 -%}
                    <option value=""{% if model_pending %} selected{% endif %} disabled>{{ 'products.buy.model_placeholder' | t }}</option>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- for v in product.variants -%}
                    <option value="{{ v.id }}"{% unless v.available %} disabled{% endunless %}{% if model_pending == false and v.id == cvar.id %} selected{% endif %}>{{ v.title | escape }}{% unless v.available %}{{ sold_suffix }}{% endunless %}</option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </span>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </noscript>

        {%- comment -%} ---------- Candy-box packs + savings meter ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if tier_count > 0 -%}
          <div class="cvc__packs" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ section.settings.packs_label | default: 'How many cases' | escape }}" data-cvm-packs>
            <span class="cvc__pack-highlight" data-cvm-pack-highlight aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {%- for b in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if b.type == 'tier' -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign t_qty = b.settings.qty | at_least: 1
                  assign t_pct = pct_arr[forloop.index0] | plus: 0
                  assign t_line = cvar.price | times: t_qty
                  assign t_off = t_line | times: t_pct | divided_by: 100.0 | floor
                  assign t_off_money = t_off | money
                  assign t_each = t_line | minus: t_off | divided_by: t_qty
                  comment
                    Ribbon: the merchant's text ([pct] is filled in), else "Save [pct]%" from the tier's own
                    percentage, so the ribbon can never disagree with the price.
                  endcomment
                  assign t_flag = b.settings.flag_label | replace: '[pct]', t_pct
                  if t_flag == blank and t_pct > 0
                    assign t_flag = 'products.product_summary.save' | t | append: ' ' | append: t_pct | append: '%'
                  endif
                -%}
                <button type="button" class="cvc__pack{% if b.settings.accent == 'teal' %} cvc__pack--teal{% endif %}" role="radio" data-cv-pack
                        aria-checked="{% if b.id == active_tier.id %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                        tabindex="{% if b.id == active_tier.id %}0{% else %}-1{% endif %}"
                        data-cv-qty="{{ t_qty }}"
                        data-cv-discount="{{ t_pct }}"
                        {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>
                  {%- if t_flag != blank -%}<span class="cvc__flag">{{ t_flag | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                  <span class="cvc__pack-name">{{ b.settings.name | escape }}</span>
                  <span class="cvc__pack-each" data-cv-tier-each="small">{{ t_each | money }}{% if t_qty > 1 %}<small>{{ 'products.buy.each' | t }}</small>{% endif %}</span>
                  <s class="cvc__pack-was" data-cv-tier-was{% unless show_compare %} hidden{% endunless %}><span class="cvc__visually-hidden">{{ 'products.price_offer.compare_at' | t }}: </span><span data-cv-tier-was-value>{{ compare_price | money }}</span></s>
                  {%- comment -%} The pack's whole saving in money, rounded down like checkout (assets/cv-product.js keeps it in step with the chosen case). {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- assign t_save_text = section.settings.pack_save_text | default: 'Save [amount]' -%}
                  <span class="cvc__pack-save" data-cv-tier-save data-template="{{ t_save_text | escape }}"{% if t_off <= 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ t_save_text | replace: '[amount]', t_off_money | escape }}</span>
                </button>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>

          {%- if max_pct > 0 -%}
            {%- liquid
              if active_off > 0
                assign active_off_money = active_off | money
                assign savings_line = section.settings.savings_text | default: '[qty] cases saves you [amount] vs buying singly' | replace: '[qty]', active_qty | replace: '[amount]', active_off_money
              elsif next_tier != nil
                assign savings_line = section.settings.savings_next_text | default: 'Choose [qty] cases to save [pct]% on each' | replace: '[qty]', next_tier.settings.qty | replace: '[pct]', next_pct
              endif
            -%}
            <div class="cvc__savings">
              <span class="cvc__meter" aria-hidden="true"><span class="cvc__meter-fill" data-cv-savings-fill style="width: {{ meter_pct }}%;"></span></span>
              <p class="cvc__savings-text" data-cv-savings aria-live="polite"
                 data-template-save="{{ section.settings.savings_text | default: '[qty] cases saves you [amount] vs buying singly' | escape }}"
                 data-template-next="{{ section.settings.savings_next_text | default: 'Choose [qty] cases to save [pct]% on each' | escape }}">{{ savings_line | escape }}</p>
            </div>
            {%- comment -%} True because the store's pack discounts count every case in the bag, whatever the design. {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if section.settings.packs_note != blank -%}
              <p class="cvc__packs-note">{{ section.settings.packs_note | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%} ---------- Mix-and-match: each case in a pack gets its own colour and phone ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if section.settings.mix_packs -%}
            {%- assign max_qty = 1 -%}
            {%- for b in section.blocks -%}{%- if b.type == 'tier' and b.settings.qty > max_qty -%}{%- assign max_qty = b.settings.qty -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
            {%- render 'cv-pack-slots', product: product, model_oi: model_oi, max_qty: max_qty, active_qty: active_qty, look: 'counter', sid: section.id,
                heading: section.settings.mix_heading, hint: section.settings.mix_hint, same_label: section.settings.mix_same, first_note: section.settings.mix_first_note -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---------- Add to bag + Buy now ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cvc__buttons">
          {%- comment -%} data-cvm-*: busy, done and error states from assets/cv-commerce-motion.js; cv-product.js owns the classes and the text. {%- endcomment -%}
          <button type="submit" class="cvc__add cv-eyes-host" id="cvAddBtn" data-cvm-btn{% unless cvar.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
            <svg class="cvc__add-check" data-cvm-icon viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5 10 17.5 19 7"/></svg>
            <span id="cvCtaLabel" data-cvm-label data-label-default="{{ add_label | escape }}">
              {%- if cvar.available -%}{{ add_label | escape }}{%- else -%}{{ 'products.buy.sold_out' | t }}{%- endif -%}
            </span>
            <span class="cvc__add-total"><span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <span id="cvTotal" data-cvm-price data-cents="{{ active_total }}">{{ active_total | money }}</span></span>
            <noscript><span class="cvc__add-total cvc__add-total--nojs"><span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {{ cvar.price | money }}</span></noscript>
            {%- render 'cv-eyes' -%}
          </button>
          {%- if section.settings.show_buy_now -%}
            <button type="button" class="cvc__buy cv-eyes-host cv-eyes-host--2" data-cv-buy-now data-cvm-btn{% unless cvar.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
              <span data-cv-buy-label data-cvm-label data-label-default="{{ buy_label | escape }}">{{ buy_label | escape }}</span>
              {%- render 'cv-eyes', count: 2 -%}
            </button>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <p class="cvc__status" id="cvStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

        {%- render 'cv-counter-blocks', blocks: section.blocks, type: 'google_rating', product: product, settings: section.settings -%}

        {%- if section.settings.dispatch_max > 0 -%}
          <p class="cvc__shipby" data-cvc-ship-by data-max-days="{{ section.settings.dispatch_max }}"
             data-template="{{ section.settings.ship_by_text | default: 'Order today, ships by [date]' | escape }}">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.6"/><path d="M12 7.3V12l3 1.9"/></svg>
            <span data-cvc-ship-by-text>{{ section.settings.ship_by_fallback | default: 'Ships in 1-3 business days' | escape }}</span>
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} The payment methods checkout really offers, from Shopify's own list of enabled types. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.show_payment_icons and shop.enabled_payment_types.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="cvc__pay">
            <p class="cvc__pay-label">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="5" y="10.5" width="14" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10.5V7.5a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg>
              <span>{{ section.settings.pay_label | default: 'Secure checkout' | escape }}</span>
            </p>
            <ul class="cvc__pay-list" role="list">
              {%- for type in shop.enabled_payment_types -%}
                <li>{{ type | payment_type_svg_tag: class: 'cvc__pay-icon' }}</li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} "Case feature" blocks this product backs up, as a tile card. Motion: assets/cv-case-features.js. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if is_case -%}{%- render 'cv-case-features', blocks: section.blocks, product: product, title: section.settings.features_title -%}{%- endif -%}

        {%- render 'cv-product-accordions',
          product: product,
          model_oi: model_oi,
          details_label: section.settings.details_label,
          brand_label: section.settings.brand_label,
          shipping_label: section.settings.shipping_label,
          shipping_text: section.settings.shipping_text,
          fits_label: section.settings.fits_label,
          damage_label: section.settings.damage_label,
          damage_text: section.settings.damage_text
        -%}
      </form>

      {%- comment -%}
        Video reviews (snippets/cv-video-reviews.liquid): this section's "Video
        review" blocks, with text from its optional "Video reviews: text" block.
        A third grid item: on desktop it sits in the photo column under the
        photo (assets/cv-pdp-video-reviews.css), in one column it follows the
        buy box. Renders nothing until this product has a clip.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign vr_block = nil
        for b in section.blocks
          if b.type == 'video_reviews'
            assign vr_block = b
            break
          endif
        endfor
        assign vr_uid = section.id | append: '-vr'
      -%}
      {%- if vr_block.settings.show_clips -%}{%- render 'cv-video-reviews', blocks: section.blocks, clip_type: 'video_review', settings: vr_block.settings, uid: vr_uid, mode: 'inline', attrs: vr_block.shopify_attributes, product: product -%}{%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} Zoom: the real photos, large, panned by pointer or finger. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if hero_image != blank -%}
    <dialog class="cvc-zoom" id="cvcZoom-{{ section.id }}" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}: {{ 'products.gallery.photos_label' | t | escape }}" data-cvc-zoom>
      <div class="cvc-zoom__frame" data-cvc-zoom-frame>
        <img
          class="cvc-zoom__img"
          src="{{ hero_image | image_url: width: 2400 }}"
          alt="{{ hero_image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
          width="{{ hero_image.width }}"
          height="{{ hero_image.height }}"
          loading="lazy"
          data-cvc-zoom-img
        >
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="cvc-zoom__btn cvc-zoom__btn--close" data-cvc-zoom-close aria-label="{{ 'products.gallery.close' | t | escape }}">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"/></svg>
      </button>
      {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
        <button type="button" class="cvc-zoom__btn cvc-zoom__btn--prev" data-cvc-zoom-step="-1" aria-label="{{ 'products.gallery.previous_photo' | t | escape }}">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 5-7 7 7 7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="cvc-zoom__btn cvc-zoom__btn--next" data-cvc-zoom-step="1" aria-label="{{ 'products.gallery.next_photo' | t | escape }}">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </button>
      {%- endif -%}
      <p class="cvc-zoom__count" data-cvc-zoom-count aria-live="polite"></p>
    </dialog>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Sticky bar whenever the Add to bag button is off screen: both buttons stay in reach. With
    "sticky_early" on it also shows before the shopper reaches the button (on a phone that is
    two screens down); off, it waits until the button has scrolled away above.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="cvc-sticky" id="cvSticky" aria-hidden="true"{% if section.settings.sticky_early %} data-sticky-early{% endif %}>
    {%- if hero_media != blank -%}
      <span class="cvc-sticky__pic">{{ hero_image | image_url: width: 120 | image_tag: width: 48, height: 48, alt: '', loading: 'lazy' }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="cvc-sticky__info">
      <span class="cvc-sticky__name">{% if short_title %}{{ design_name | escape }}{% else %}{{ product.title | escape }}{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="cvc-sticky__meta"><span class="cvc-sticky__variant"><span data-cv-opt-out-sticky>{{ variant_label | escape }}</span> · </span><b id="cvStickyTotal" data-cvm-price data-cents="{{ active_total }}">{{ active_total | money }}</b></span>
    </div>
    <div class="cvc-sticky__buttons">
      <button type="button" class="cvc-sticky__add cv-eyes-host" id="cvStickyBtn" data-cvm-btn tabindex="-1">{{ sticky_label | escape }}{%- render 'cv-eyes' -%}</button>
      {%- if section.settings.show_buy_now -%}
        <button type="button" class="cvc-sticky__buy cv-eyes-host cv-eyes-host--2" data-cv-buy-now data-cvm-btn tabindex="-1">{{ buy_label | escape }}{%- render 'cv-eyes', count: 2 -%}</button>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- render 'cv-product-schema', product: product, has_rating: has_rating, rating_value: rating_value, rating_count: rating_count -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product: shop counter",
  "tag": "div",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "crumb_label", "label": "Breadcrumb shop label", "default": "Cases", "info": "Used when the product isn't viewed inside a collection." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "vendor_suffix", "label": "Vendor ticket suffix", "default": "Cases", "info": "Shown after the vendor name, for example Casify Cases." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "zoom_label", "label": "Zoom chip", "default": "View larger" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "model_first", "label": "Open on the 3D view", "default": true, "info": "When the product has a 3D model, it is the first photo ticket and the stage opens on it. Off: the 3D ticket comes second and opens when chosen." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Price offer" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "compare_price_fallback", "label": "Fallback compare-at price", "info": "Used only when the selected variant has no higher compare-at price, and only for shoppers paying in the shop currency. Use a price the case really sold at." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Rating" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_price_saving", "label": "Show the \"You save\" line", "default": true, "info": "Under the title, when the variant has a real compare-at price. Turn off if the \"Rating, price & pitch\" block already shows the saving." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_rating", "label": "Show rating row", "default": true, "info": "Counts this product's Judge.me reviews from verified buyers only." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "reviews_anchor", "label": "Reviews section anchor", "default": "cvc-reviews" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Main image awning" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_awning", "label": "Hang a shop awning over the main photo", "default": false, "info": "A 3D fabric canopy that unrolls on load and sways in the breeze. Flat for shoppers who prefer reduced motion." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "awning_stripes", "label": "Stripes", "min": 8, "max": 24, "step": 2, "default": 16 },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "awning_tone",
      "label": "Awning colour",
      "options": [
        { "value": "red", "label": "Candy red and cream" },
        { "value": "teal", "label": "Teal and cream" }
      ],
      "default": "red",
      "info": "The colour it starts in."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_price_tag", "label": "Hanging price tag by the title", "default": true, "info": "The brass tag with the price and a red \"% off\" burst. Off, the price still shows under the title." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_photo_price", "label": "Price tag on the photo", "default": false, "info": "A 3D price tag hangs from the awning and flips when the variant changes. Shows a struck-through price and saving only when the variant has a real compare-at price." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "awning_swipe", "label": "Let shoppers swipe to switch red and teal", "default": true, "info": "A sideways scroll, swipe or drag over the awning slides it to the other colour." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_customer_proof", "label": "Show the customer proof text", "default": false, "info": "Shown only when you can back it. Not in the store's evidence on hand. Off: the row reads No reviews yet." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "empty_rating_text", "label": "Customer proof text", "default": "No reviews yet", "info": "Shown before this product has its own reviews, only while the box above is ticked." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "empty_rating_link", "label": "No reviews link", "default": "Write the first review" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Google and Trustpilot ratings" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Shown under the price. The store rating is your Google and Trustpilot reviews combined and is labelled that way on the page. The Trustpilot fields are for a Trustpilot-only score and can stay empty. A ticket shows only when its rating is filled in. Update the numbers when they change." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_external_review_badges", "label": "Show Google and Trustpilot ratings", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_store_rating", "label": "These store ratings match the shop's review pages", "default": false, "info": "Shown only when you can back it. Not in the store's evidence on hand. Tick only when the numbers below are the real ones (the documented store rating is 4.9 from 952 reviews on Trustpilot and Google). Off hides the tickets, the Google strip and the store rating under the title." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "external_review_rating", "label": "Store rating (Google and Trustpilot combined)", "info": "For example 4.9. Shown as \"Google and Trustpilot\". Also used for the stars under the title while a product has no reviews of its own." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "external_review_count", "label": "Store review count (Google and Trustpilot combined)", "info": "For example 952." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "google_reviews_url", "label": "Store rating link", "info": "Optional. Opens your reviews page in a new tab." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "trustpilot_rating", "label": "Trustpilot rating", "info": "Your TrustScore, for example 4.5." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "trustpilot_review_count", "label": "Trustpilot review count" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "trustpilot_url", "label": "Trustpilot page link", "info": "Optional. Opens your Trustpilot page in a new tab." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Low stock" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "low_stock_threshold", "label": "Show below this many left", "min": 0, "max": 20, "step": 1, "default": 10, "info": "Reads the chosen variant's real Shopify inventory count. Only shows for variants Shopify tracks and that stop selling at zero, so the number is always true. Set 0 to turn off." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "low_stock_text", "label": "Low stock line", "default": "Only [qty] left in this style" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "stock_style",
      "label": "Low stock style",
      "options": [
        { "value": "pill", "label": "Yellow pill with blinking dot" },
        { "value": "line", "label": "Plain red line" }
      ],
      "default": "pill"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Options" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "option_label", "label": "Style label", "default": "Style", "info": "Label for the product's other option. Leave empty to use the option's own name." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "model_label", "label": "Model label", "default": "Model" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "packs_label", "label": "Packs label (screen readers)", "default": "How many cases" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "savings_text", "label": "Savings line", "default": "[qty] cases saves you [amount] vs buying singly", "info": "[qty] and [amount] are filled in from the chosen pack." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "savings_next_text", "label": "Savings line on a single case", "default": "Choose [qty] cases to save [pct]% on each", "info": "[qty] and [pct] come from the next pack up." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "pack_save_text", "label": "Pack saving pill", "default": "Save [amount]", "info": "On each pack of 2 or more. [amount] is the whole pack's saving, rounded down to the cent like checkout." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "packs_note", "label": "Note under the packs", "default": "Mix any designs. Every case in your bag counts toward the pack price.", "info": "True only while the store's pack discounts count any cases in the bag. Leave empty to hide." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Mix-and-match packs" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "mix_packs", "label": "Let each case in a pack have its own colour and phone", "default": true, "info": "Works with the store's pack discounts, which count any cases in the bag." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mix_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Your [qty] cases", "info": "[qty] is the pack size." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mix_hint", "label": "Hint", "default": "Pick a colour and phone for each case. Mix them however you like." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mix_first_note", "label": "Note beside case 1", "default": "chosen above" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mix_same", "label": "Match case 1 link", "default": "Same as case 1" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Buttons" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Add to bag label", "default": "Add to bag" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_buy_now", "label": "Show Buy now", "default": true, "info": "Adds the chosen case and pack to the bag and goes straight to checkout." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "buy_label", "label": "Buy now label", "default": "Buy now" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "sticky_cta", "label": "Sticky bar add label", "default": "Add to bag" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "sticky_early", "label": "Show the sticky bar before Add to bag is reached", "info": "On phones the button sits below the photos and options; this keeps it in reach from the first screen.", "default": true },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Case type" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "short_title", "label": "Short title", "info": "The design name large, with the line below under it. Only on cases whose type (Tough, Magnetic or Clear) the product's tags or title name.", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title_sub", "label": "Line under the short title", "default": "Phone case for [brands]", "info": "[brands] comes from the product's phone models: iPhone, Samsung, Pixel." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "case_label", "label": "Case type label", "default": "[type] case", "info": "Shown above the title. [type] is tough, magnetic or clear." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "chips_tough", "label": "Tough case chips", "default": "Two layers, Glossy or matte, Wireless charging", "info": "Separate with commas. Only facts true for every Tough case." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "chips_magnetic", "label": "Magnetic case chips", "default": "MagSafe magnet, Two layers, Glossy or matte", "info": "Separate with commas. Only facts true for every Magnetic case." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "chips_clear", "label": "Clear case chips", "default": "Slim fit, Soft clear sides, Wireless charging", "info": "Separate with commas. Only facts true for every Clear case." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_case_switcher", "label": "Case switcher", "info": "This design as Tough, Magnetic and Clear: products with the same design name (the title before \" Phone Case\").", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "switcher_label", "label": "Case switcher label", "default": "Case" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Ship-by date" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "dispatch_max", "label": "Latest dispatch, business days", "min": 0, "max": 10, "step": 1, "default": 3, "info": "The date shown is today plus this many business days (Monday to Friday). Set 0 to hide the line." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ship_by_text", "label": "Ship-by line", "default": "Order today, ships by [date]" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ship_by_fallback", "label": "Line before the date is worked out", "default": "Ships in 1-3 business days" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Payment" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_payment_icons", "label": "Show payment icons", "default": true, "info": "The payment methods enabled in Shopify, under the ship-by line." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "pay_label", "label": "Payment label", "default": "Secure checkout" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Case features" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Add a \"Case feature\" block for each feature. The card under the ship-by line shows up to six, and only the ones this product matches." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "features_title", "label": "Card heading", "default": "Built into this case", "info": "Leave empty for no heading." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Accordions" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "details_label", "label": "Details label", "default": "Details" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "brand_label", "label": "Brand label", "default": "Brand" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "shipping_label", "label": "Shipping label", "default": "Shipping & returns" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "shipping_text", "label": "Shipping & returns", "default": "<p>Free shipping on every order. Each case is printed after you order, which takes up to 10 business days, then ships with tracking.</p>", "info": "State only what is true for every order." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fits_label", "label": "Phone list label", "default": "Fits these phones", "info": "Lists every phone model this case is made for. Leave empty to hide." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "damage_label", "label": "Damage cover label", "default": "Damage cover" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "damage_text", "label": "Damage cover", "info": "Leave empty to hide. State only what the return policy promises." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "@app" },
    {
      "type": "tier",
      "name": "Pack tier",
      "limit": 4,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "number", "id": "qty", "label": "Cases", "default": 1 },
        { "type": "range", "id": "discount_pct", "label": "Discount per case", "min": 0, "max": 60, "step": 1, "unit": "%", "default": 0, "info": "Must match an automatic discount in Shopify admin > Discounts, or checkout will charge a different price than the page shows." },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "use_theme_pct", "label": "Use the pack discount from theme settings", "default": true, "info": "For 2 or 3 cases, the percentage comes from Theme settings > Packs and shipping, so every page shows the same discount. Off: the percentage above is used." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Label", "default": "1 case" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "flag_label", "label": "Ribbon", "info": "Optional. Leave empty for Save [pct]% from this pack's discount. [pct] is filled in. Keep it true, for example Best value." },
        { "type": "select", "id": "accent", "label": "Box colour", "default": "red", "options": [ { "value": "red", "label": "Red stripes" }, { "value": "teal", "label": "Teal stripes" } ] },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "default_checked", "label": "Selected by default", "default": false }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "service",
      "name": "Service fact",
      "limit": 3,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon", "default": "truck", "options": [ { "value": "truck", "label": "Truck" }, { "value": "returns", "label": "Returns" }, { "value": "box", "label": "Box" } ] },
        { "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Text", "default": "Free shipping", "info": "Only facts true for every order." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "feature",
      "name": "Case feature",
      "limit": 12,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "One tile on the features card. It shows only on products that match, so each line stays true for the case it sits under." },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "icon",
          "label": "Icon",
          "default": "drop",
          "options": [
            { "value": "drop", "label": "Drop protection" },
            { "value": "layers", "label": "Shell and liner" },
            { "value": "magsafe", "label": "MagSafe charging" },
            { "value": "finish", "label": "Glossy finish" },
            { "value": "button", "label": "Camera button" },
            { "value": "stand", "label": "Kickstand" },
            { "value": "fit", "label": "Printed to fit" }
          ]
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Text", "info": "Say only what the matching cases really do. Empty: the tile is hidden." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "keywords", "label": "Show on products matching", "info": "Comma-separated words looked for in the product's title, type, vendor and option values, for example: tough, shockproof. Leave empty to show on every product." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "tag", "label": "Product tag override", "info": "Optional, for example feature-stand. Products with this tag always show the tile; products tagged no-feature-stand never do." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "summary",
      "name": "Rating, price & pitch",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Shows under the product title: stars, rating and review count, then price, the variant's real compare-at price and saving, then a one-line pitch. The stars count only this product's Judge.me reviews from verified buyers." },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "rating_source",
          "label": "Rating",
          "options": [
            { "value": "auto", "label": "Verified Judge.me reviews" },
            { "value": "product", "label": "Verified reviews only" },
            { "value": "store", "label": "Verified reviews (old store option)" }
          ],
          "default": "auto",
          "info": "Every choice now shows the same thing: this product's Judge.me reviews from verified buyers."
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "reviews_article", "label": "Review widget blog post (no longer used)", "default": "customer-reviews/reviews" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "empty_label", "label": "Text with no reviews yet", "default": "Be the first to review", "info": "Links to the reviews section. Leave empty to hide." },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_price", "label": "Show price, compare-at price and saving", "default": true },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "save_style",
          "label": "Saving",
          "options": [
            { "value": "amount", "label": "Amount, e.g. Save $10.00" },
            { "value": "percent", "label": "Percent, e.g. Save 17%" }
          ],
          "default": "amount"
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "tagline", "label": "Pitch line", "info": "Keep it true for every product it shows on." },
        { "type": "product_list", "id": "pitch_products", "label": "Show the pitch only on", "limit": 50, "info": "Leave empty to show it on every product using this template." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "tagline_metafield", "label": "Pitch metafield (namespace.key)", "info": "Optional. A product's own text metafield replaces the pitch line, e.g. custom.pitch." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "google_rating",
      "name": "Google rating",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Shows under the Add to bag button. Hidden until a rating is entered." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "rating", "label": "Google rating", "info": "Your current rating from your Google Business Profile, e.g. 4.4." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "review_count", "label": "Google review count", "info": "Optional." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "headline", "label": "Short quote", "info": "Optional. A word or phrase taken from a real Google review, e.g. Amazing." },
        { "type": "url", "id": "reviews_url", "label": "Google reviews link", "info": "Optional. Opens your Google reviews in a new tab." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sales_note",
      "name": "Sales note",
      "limit": 2,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Shows a real sales number, e.g. \"18 sold this week\": the product's own count (Shopify admin → the product → \"Sold this week\" / \"Total sold\"), or the number typed here. Hidden when there is no number." },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "style",
          "label": "Style",
          "options": [
            { "value": "pill", "label": "Pill with blinking dot" },
            { "value": "rocket", "label": "Rocket line with pulsing number" }
          ],
          "default": "pill"
        },
        { "type": "number", "id": "count", "label": "Number", "info": "Used only on the products listed below that have no count of their own. Use a real number, and word the text to match what it counts." },
        { "type": "product_list", "id": "typed_count_products", "label": "Use the typed number only on", "limit": 50, "info": "Shown only when you can back it. Not in the store's evidence on hand. Empty: the note shows only each product's own count field." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "metafield", "label": "Product count field (namespace.key)", "default": "custom.sold_recently", "info": "Each product's own number, set in Shopify admin on the product: custom.sold_recently is \"Sold this week\", custom.total_sold is \"Total sold\". It replaces the number above on that product." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Text", "default": "[count] sold this week", "info": "[count] is the metafield value. Match the wording to what the number really counts, e.g. \"Hurry up! [count] items have been sold\" for an all-time total." },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "round_to",
          "label": "Round down",
          "options": [
            { "value": "1", "label": "Exact number" },
            { "value": "10", "label": "To tens, e.g. 530+" },
            { "value": "50", "label": "To fifties, e.g. 500+" },
            { "value": "100", "label": "To hundreds, e.g. 500+" }
          ],
          "default": "1",
          "info": "Rounds down and adds +, so the claim never overstates."
        },
        { "type": "range", "id": "min_count", "label": "Hide below", "min": 1, "max": 50, "step": 1, "default": 5, "info": "Hides the note when the number is smaller than this." },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "tone",
          "label": "Pill colour",
          "options": [
            { "value": "gold", "label": "Yellow" },
            { "value": "teal", "label": "Teal" }
          ],
          "default": "gold"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "spec_meter",
      "name": "Protection meter",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Two bar meters under the style swatches: impact protection with its drop height, and thickness. A product's own metafields replace these numbers: custom.impact_level and custom.thickness_level (whole numbers), custom.drop_height (text)." },
        { "type": "product_list", "id": "products", "label": "Show only on", "limit": 50, "info": "Leave empty to show it on every product using this template. Keep the numbers true for every product it shows on." },
        { "type": "range", "id": "segments", "label": "Bars per meter", "min": 4, "max": 10, "step": 1, "default": 6 },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "tone",
          "label": "Bar colour",
          "options": [
            { "value": "candy", "label": "Red impact, teal thickness" },
            { "value": "teal", "label": "Teal" },
            { "value": "red", "label": "Candy red" },
            { "value": "blue", "label": "Blue" }
          ],
          "default": "candy"
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "pattern",
          "label": "Bar pattern",
          "options": [
            { "value": "stripes", "label": "Candy stripes" },
            { "value": "solid", "label": "Solid" }
          ],
          "default": "stripes",
          "info": "The stripes drift slowly while the meter is on screen."
        },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_sweets", "label": "Wrapped sweet at the end of each bar", "default": true },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "drop_test", "label": "Drop a 3D phone onto the impact bar", "default": true, "info": "Plays when the meter comes into view, and again on hover or tap. Off for shoppers who prefer reduced motion." },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Impact" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "impact_label", "label": "Label", "default": "Impact Level" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "impact_value", "label": "Drop height", "info": "Shown only when you can back it. Not in the store's evidence on hand. Shown beside the label. Leave empty to hide." },
        { "type": "range", "id": "impact_level", "label": "Filled bars", "min": 0, "max": 10, "step": 1, "default": 0 },
        { "type": "text", "id": "impact_min", "label": "Low end", "default": "Min." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "impact_max", "label": "High end", "default": "Max." },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Thickness" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "thickness_label", "label": "Label", "default": "Thickness" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "thickness_value", "label": "Measurement", "info": "Optional, shown beside the label, for example 1.6mm." },
        { "type": "range", "id": "thickness_level", "label": "Filled bars", "min": 0, "max": 10, "step": 1, "default": 0 },
        { "type": "text", "id": "thickness_min", "label": "Low end", "default": "Slim" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "thickness_max", "label": "High end", "default": "Sturdy" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "video_reviews",
      "name": "Video reviews: text",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Customer video reviews show under the product photo. Add a \"Video review\" block for each clip; the row appears once this product has one. This block only changes the words." },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_clips", "label": "Show customer clips", "default": false, "info": "Shown only when you can back it. Not in the store's evidence on hand. Tick only for real clips from real buyers: names, stars and quotes must be theirs." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Case clips" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "lede", "label": "Text", "info": "Optional line under the heading." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "hint", "label": "Hint", "default": "Tap a clip for sound and the full review" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "verified_label", "label": "Verified badge", "default": "Verified buyer", "info": "Shows only on clips ticked Verified buyer, after finding their order." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "bought_label", "label": "Phone and colour label", "default": "Filmed on" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "anon_label", "label": "Name when none is given", "default": "Customer" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "submit_label", "label": "Send-a-clip link", "default": "Filmed yours? Send it in" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "submit_url", "label": "Send-a-clip page", "info": "The link shows only when a page is chosen, for example your contact page." },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Shopping panel" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "model_label", "label": "Phone label", "default": "Your phone" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "model_placeholder", "label": "Phone placeholder", "default": "Select your phone model" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "pick_model_text", "label": "Reminder when no phone is chosen", "default": "Pick your phone model first, so the case fits." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Add to bag" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "cta_pack_label", "label": "Button label for a pack", "default": "Add [qty] cases", "info": "[qty] is the number of cases in the pack chosen in the buy box." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "video_review",
      "name": "Video review",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "One clip a customer sent you, shown under the product photo. Type their name, rating and words exactly as they gave them." },
        { "type": "video", "id": "video", "label": "Video", "info": "Upload the customer's clip. Upright 9:16 works best." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "mp4_url", "label": "Or a direct MP4 link", "info": "Used when no video is uploaded." },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "poster", "label": "Cover image", "info": "Optional. Without one, the video's own first frame is used. A cover with no video shows as a photo review." },
        { "type": "header", "content": "The review" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Customer name", "info": "As they want it shown, for example \"Sam R.\"" },
        { "type": "range", "id": "stars", "label": "Their star rating", "min": 1, "max": 5, "step": 1, "default": 5 },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Quote on the clip", "info": "A short line from their review." },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Full review", "info": "Shown when the clip is opened." },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "verified", "label": "Verified buyer", "default": false, "info": "Tick only after finding their order." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "date", "label": "Date", "info": "Optional, for example \"September 2026\"." },
        { "type": "header", "content": "The case in the clip" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "phone", "label": "Phone", "info": "For example \"iPhone 17 Pro\"." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "colour", "label": "Colour", "info": "Write it exactly as the product's colour option, and the player offers \"Choose this colour\"." },
        { "type": "product", "id": "product", "label": "Only show on", "info": "Leave blank to show this clip on every product that uses this template." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Product: shop counter",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "tier", "settings": { "qty": 1, "discount_pct": 0, "name": "1 case" } },
        { "type": "tier", "settings": { "qty": 2, "discount_pct": 18, "name": "2 cases", "default_checked": true } },
        { "type": "tier", "settings": { "qty": 3, "discount_pct": 31, "name": "3 cases", "flag_label": "Best value", "accent": "teal" } },
        { "type": "service", "settings": { "icon": "truck", "text": "Free shipping" } },
        { "type": "service", "settings": { "icon": "returns", "text": "30-day returns" } },
        { "type": "service", "settings": { "icon": "box", "text": "Ships in 1-3 business days" } }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": { "templates": ["product"] }
}
{% endschema %}
